the us's longest war is over the  pentagon says the last american troops  have been flown out of afghanistan after  a 20-year mission the departure follows  two weeks of chaotic and desperate  scenes in and around kabul airport as  thousands of foreign nationals and  afghan citizens tried to flee  the taliban have now proclaimed  afghanistan's full independence  this time the gunfire heard of a kabul  was different  with the american troops gone people  began celebrating their departure  the u.s military worked all day monday  for the final withdrawal it was one  minute before midnight that the last  plane took off on august 31 america's  longest war drew to a close a new  chapter of america's engagement with  afghanistan has begun  it's one in which we will lead with our  diplomacy  the military mission is over  a new diplomatic mission has begun  because of security concerns secretary  of state lincoln said the u.s embassy in  kabul will stay vacant and its diplomats  will work from qatar  it was also security concerns and a  successful attack on kabul airport why  the u.s government rushed to meet the  deadline at a cost  look there's a lot of heartbreak  associated with this departure we did  not get everybody out that we wanted to  get out but i think if we stayed another  10 days louie we wouldn't have gotten  everybody out that we wanted to get out  and there still would have been people  who would have been disappointed  to those who were left behind secretary  blinken made a promise  more than half the world's countries  have joined us in insisting that the  taliban let people travel outside  afghanistan freely  as of today  more than 100 countries have said that  they expect the taliban to honor travel  authorizations by our countries  we will hold the taliban to their  commitment on freedom of movement for  foreign nationals visa holders at risk  afghans  the taliban said on twitter after the  americans left afghanistan gained full  independence  let's cross to kabul now where  journalist france marty is standing by  france after 20 years the last american  soldier has now left afghanistan is  there a sense of change in kabul this  morning  not that much yesterday night there was  like celebratory gunfire as i've never  heard it before but this was of course  of the taliban forces um in the  city um other people were like uh rather  very or someone told me that his  children were like afraid of the  celebratory gunfire i was just in the  city center it looks more or less normal  not that many people on the street but  shops are open  um there is there was no sense of like  uh  um  as jubilant sense uh people were like  normally going about their work some  told me that they are worried  because like business is bad  no one buys anything no one sells  anything um refugees are still camping  out in the park  so there wasn't that there wasn't like a  scene of celebration today in the  morning in the city center  there had been desperate scenes of  course at kabul airport are the taliban  now in control there is the airport  still operational  and polymon have entered the airport  like and posted like many uh videos on  social media  of of their forces inside the airport  some taliban also made brief statements  in the airport um one taliban official  told uh local channel tolo news that  they have prepared for this that they  will be able to run the airport however  at the moment this can't be assessed uh  completely  plus the taliban themselves can't like  run  air control and everything that is  needed to operate an airport uh but  there are uh their reports uh that they  will get support from qatar and turkey  um to to again make the airport  operational when this will be the case  remains to be seen  what about foreign nationals friends who  still want to leave the country will  they be able to get out are they in  danger  the taliban have  several times assured that people with  the right travel documents are allowed  to depart the country  of course now you have the problem there  are like no international flights from  carnival airport or any other airport um  land border crossings are like only  partly open  for foreign national passport holders  should be possible to like get over land  border crossings um but this is like so  far everyone tried to get on evacuation  flights from kabul airport and now it  remains to be seen how difficult or easy  the taliban will make it for people to  leave  this is a momentous occasion for the  taliban they have declared now that  afghanistan is independent  uh what can we expect from the taliban  in the coming days  it is really hard to say the taliban  have uh not only since they took over  kabul already before they've already  always been vague about what they  exactly want to do they always repeat  that they want a islamic system meaning  that the constitution of the former or  like current islamic republic of  afghanistan  was not islamic enough so they certainly  want to change a lot but how exactly  they will go about it how they will do  this is still unclear  several reports suggested that they  might deliberately have wanted to make  clear announcement until the last  american forces left so it can be  expected that within the next days or  maybe even today  they will announce something and give  more clarity but so far  they have really not said much what they  want to do  france thank you very much that was  journalist franz marty in kabul
 

